      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I believe they are required by GDPR to ask the user in this case. See article 5 GDPR on \"data minimization\":\n\n\"Personal data shall be (...) collected for specified, explicit and legitimate purposes and not further processed in a manner that is incompatible with those purposes\"\n\nAs soon as the age is verified, i do not see any legitimate purpose in storing the ID.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-12-03T01:13:07.003Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "In last Age Verification FAQ\n\nhttps://ask.vrchat.com/t/age-verification-faq/28458\n\n- It been confirmed that User's private info will be stored by Persona for indefinitely / some time.\n\n- It been mentioned that **Users might ask VRChat and/or Persona to delete their data**.\n\nHowever, I assume, this information will be silent and not spread far away from this forum thread, **if** UI for verification process would not **explicitly say** to the verifying user that they able to ask for their data deletion right after verification done.\n\nIt would be even better, if the process **asks the user explicitly**:\n\n*Do you want to hold your information, or we should inform Persona that you want to delete it?*\n\nOr something like that.",
